  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "A note: native selection on regular systems, and why three places",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "A self-contained note (LaTeX, 5 pages) with a review package on native selection: which Boolean law on regular systems has failures recognisable in polynomial time while its count is #P-hard. It states, with pointers to the repository proofs: the knot's coupling on its spaces is easy exactly at lam in {0, 1, -1, -3, oo}; not-all-equal is the only three-place law with mutual selection unless NP-complete problems are polynomial (pinning); parity's failures are recognisable but local, its weighted family #P-hard except at six points, also on its failing systems (the corrected analysis, with the withdrawn claim recorded); at four places signed not-all-equal never fails (Seymour, Thomassen) and every class that fails builds equality, so only five weak classes could be mutually selecting; the knot's spaces compose only through hubs, and hub-free failing composition is parity. The note adds no claim beyond the cited proofs; replay.py reruns all sixteen cited checks, independent.py recomputes nine headline claims in fresh code, and check.py ties every quoted number.",
